   "author_display_name": "Gopi",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/28040485",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2015-01-20T08:16:37Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2015-01-20T08:27:44Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2015-01-20T08:27:44Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>Memory leak can easily be produced</p>\n\n<pre><code>void func()\n{\n  int *ptr = malloc(sizeof(int) * 1000);\n  return;\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>You are not freeing the memory allocated to the pointer <code>ptr</code> and hence there is a memory leak because this allocated memory is not available for other applications and eventually if you keep doing this then you run out of memory.Like</p>\n\n<pre><code>while(1)\n{\n   int *ptr = malloc(sizeof(int) * 1000);\n}\n</code></pre>\n"
  },
